Subset notes  :
    | Problem                   | Example                       | Prevented by                                      |
    | ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
    | Reusing the same element  | `[1,1]`                       | `i + 1`                                           |
    | Different ordering        | `[1,2]` vs `[2,1]`            | Always move forward                               |
    | Duplicate values in input | `[2]` from two different `2`s | `if (i > index && nums[i] == nums[i-1]) continue` |

SUBSET       → start + take/skip
COMBINATION  → start + choose forward
PERMUTATION  → used[] + choose unused

Every new backtrack()(recursive) call starts its own for loop with i = 0 when there is no index passed in arguments

|                            | Subset  | Combination | Permutation     |
| -------------------------- | ------- | ----------- | --------------- |
| Order matters?             | ❌       | ❌           | ✅            |
| Size                       | Any     | Exactly `k` | Usually all `n`  |
| Move forward?              | ✅       | ✅           | ❌            |
| Main control               | `start` | `start`     | `used[]`         |
| Can choose previous index? | ❌       | ❌           | ✅ if unused   |
| `[1,2]` and `[2,1]`        | Same    | Same        | **Different**    |
